## Golden rules (always)

1. **Never push to `<PROTECTED_BRANCH>` without the project owner's explicit approval.**
2. Always start on `<DEFAULT_DEV_BRANCH>`. Run `<BUILD_COMMAND>` before commit.
3. Don't refactor outside the task. Preserve existing behavior unless asked.
4. For data changes: trace UI → API → DB → tests before touching.
5. <PROJECT_SPECIFIC_GOLDEN_RULE>
6. Don't read every doc. Use the routing map below.
7. **Before editing any file, the relevant `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md` will auto-load if the file path matches its `applyTo:` glob. Verify the rule loaded; if not, read it manually.**
8. **Multi-agent handoffs use a structured schema** — see `docs/ai-context/HANDOFF_SCHEMA.md`. The `@<PROJECT_SLUG>-orchestrator` agent emits outbound `handoff:` YAML; specialists return `return:` YAML. **No evidence, no claim.**
9. **Corrections harden into instruction files.** If the owner corrected a *recurring* pattern this turn, end the turn by drafting a one-line patch to the right `.github/instructions/<domain>.instructions.md` and ask for approval. Never say "I'll remember" — any memory the IDE or CLI keeps is machine-local and invisible to every other agent and teammate.
10. **Deferred work must be written, not spoken.** Any "later" / follow-up / known gap named in a summary is appended to `docs/<AREA>_BACKLOG.md` (what / why / effort / revisit-when) before the turn ends.
11. **Every production push freshens the docs — same turn, no exceptions.** `<CHANGELOG_PATH>` (the anchor), the affected orientation map(s), the affected instruction files, and `docs/ai-context/PROJECT.md` §3 if the production state changed. (Enforced by the `agentStop` doc-freshness hook if `.github/hooks/` is installed — see `docs/ai-context/HOOKS.md`.)
12. **One name per concept.** `docs/ai-context/GLOSSARY.md` is a rule file; adding a new name for an existing concept is a defect.

## Mandatory workflow (every non-trivial task)

1. Restate the task.
2. Identify affected roles (<LIST_OF_ROLES>).
3. Read `docs/ai-context/PROJECT.md` (current truth — especially §3, what is live where) and `docs/ai-context/INDEX.md`. Skim `docs/ai-context/LEARNINGS.md` §D (agent corrections) before the first edit.
4. Read only the minimum docs flagged for this task (50–150 lines each).
5. Verify that path-matching `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md` auto-loaded.
6. For medium/complex tasks, invoke `@<PROJECT_SLUG>-orchestrator` in Copilot Chat. For narrow domain work, invoke the relevant `@<specialist>` directly.
6.5. **Handoff format.** Orchestrator → specialist delegations MUST use the outbound `handoff:` YAML block from `docs/ai-context/HANDOFF_SCHEMA.md`. Specialists MUST validate it (refuse if missing/vague) and return the inbound `return:` block.
7. Inspect code before proposing changes.
8. Smallest safe change.
9. Run relevant checks (<TEST_COMMAND>, build, etc.). Verification follows the proof ladder in `.github/skills/<PROJECT_SLUG>-engineering/SKILL.md` (a green build is evidence, not proof).
10. **Definition of done:** report changed files, checks run with results, risks, follow-ups (written to a backlog), AND the list of `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md` files that applied to your edits.

